--- Repro (Admin order-edit, order 91216, worktree backend :8721) ---
GET  /admin/order/edit-order/91216        -> 200 (enters edit mode, session('order_cart') set)
POST /admin/order/add-to-cart {cart_item_key:0, id:112, item_type:item, order_id:91216, quantity:-1}
     -> 200 {"data":2}   (accepted into session cart uncritically — no server-side guard here either,
                          matches the POS addToCart()/updateQuantity() pattern already documented
                          in NEARS-3224's separate bug-pos-tax-recalc-500... note)
GET  /admin/order/update/91216            -> HTTP 500 "Something went wrong"
     (the FINAL submit action — this is the step AC7 asks to observe a clean
      quantity/invalid_quantity 403 on for the order-edit caller)

Root cause: Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Admin/OrderController.php::update() (~line 1357-1376):
    $order_details = $this->orderDetailBuilder->build($cart, new EditOrderContext(null, $store));
        foreach($order_details['order_details'] as $key => $order_de){   <- indexes BEFORE the check
            ...
        }
    if (data_get($order_details, 'status_code') === 403) { ... return response()->json(...); }
When build() returns the short error array (no 'order_details' key) for a non-positive quantity,
the foreach on line ~1359 throws "Undefined array key 'order_details'" (ErrorException, Laravel
converts the PHP warning to a hard throw) BEFORE execution ever reaches the correct status_code
check a few lines below — so the clean 403/quantity JSON never gets returned to the caller; the
operator sees a raw 500 instead.

CORRECTED classification (pre-existing, not this ticket's own defect): checked
Admin/app/Traits/PlaceNewOrder.php @ a47c1bb32 (pre-refactor Admin/OrderController.php::update()) —
the IDENTICAL ordering (foreach($order_details['order_details']...) before the status_code check)
already existed verbatim pre-refactor. And makeEditOrderDetails() (the pre-refactor callee)
already had pre-existing 'not_found' (empty cart) / 'different_stores' / 'prescription' guards
returning the SAME short error-array shape — so this exact update() crash was ALREADY reachable
pre-ticket (e.g. tampering a cart line's store id, or a prescription item with no attachment).
This ticket's new non-positive-quantity guard is one more (previously nonexistent for order-edit)
trigger for an already-broken caller-side check, not a new introduction.

Filed as regression_bug (pre-existing, unrelated to this ticket's own correctness) — does not
affect this run's verdict per the QA-agent lane rules. Flagged prominently because it means AC7's
literal "order-edit rejects a non-positive line quantity with the existing error code" could NOT
be cleanly demonstrated for the Admin order-edit caller specifically — what actually surfaces to
an operator today is a generic 500, not the intended quantity/invalid_quantity error. The
UNDERLYING GUARD LOGIC is correct (OrderDetailBuilder::buildForEdit does return the right 403
shape, confirmed by the fact update() crashes exactly at the moment it tries to read the WRONG
key off that very shape) — the gap is entirely in this pre-existing unguarded caller.
